   "text": {
    "L1": "An estimate helps us check a total before doing exact addition.",
    "L2": "It is not a random guess: round each price, then add the rounded numbers.",
    "L3": "For the cap, bottle and torch, round ₹185 to ₹200, ₹122 to ₹100, and ₹89 to ₹100.",
    "L4": "Now add: ₹200 plus ₹100 plus ₹100 is about ₹400.",
    "L5": "₹400 is well below ₹500, so the money is enough. The exact total is ₹396, close to the estimate.",
    "L6": "An estimate uses rounded numbers, so it need not equal the exact answer.",
    "L7": "If every price was rounded up, the real total is less than the estimate; if rounded down, it is more.",
    "L8": "When an estimate is right at the money limit, calculate the exact total before deciding."
   },
